.* TCPADM: the task menu for TCP/IP administration.
:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) COPYRIGHT QUARTZ SYSTEMS 2026.
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE='CHAR 2'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=OPTION CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=PANELID CLASS=NAMECL VALUE='TCPADM'.
:KEYL NAME=MENUKEYS.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F1 ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F4 ACTION='RETURN 4'.F4=Prompt
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION=RETRIEVE.F9=Retrieve
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=TCPADM HELP=HLPTCPADM KEYL=MENUKEYS ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=SYSNAM PANELID=PANELID.TCP/IP Administration
:MENU DEPTH='*' SCROLL=YES OPTIONS=OPTION.Select one of the following:
:MENUI OPTION=1 ACTION='CMD CFGTCP'.Configure TCP/IP
:MENUI OPTION=2 ACTION='CMD CFGTCPAPP'.Configure TCP/IP applications
:MENUI OPTION=7 ACTION='CMD NETSTAT'.Work with TCP/IP network status
:MENUI OPTION=8 ACTION='CMD ?PING'.Verify TCP/IP connection
:MENUI OPTION=9 ACTION='CMD ?STRTCPFTP'.Start TCP/IP FTP session
:MENUI OPTION=10 ACTION='CMD ?STRTCPTELN'.Start TCP/IP TELNET session
:MENUI OPTION=11 ACTION='CMD ?SNDTCPSPLF'.Send TCP/IP spooled file
:MENUI OPTION=20 ACTION='CMD WRKACTJOB SBS(QSYSWRK)'.Work with TCP/IP jobs in QSYSWRK subsystem
:EMENU.
:CMDLINE SIZE=LONG.Selection or command
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=HLPTCPADM.TCP/IP Administration - Help
:P.The TCP/IP stack and its servers: their configuration, their status and
the clients that use them.
:P.Type an option number or a command and press Enter. F4 prompts the
command, F9 brings the previous one back, F12 returns to the menu shown
before this one.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
